{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"9ad3e5d9-73ef-4c78-8d48-27853119f4e3","status":"SUCCESS","response":"The configuration precedence bug in [config_loader.py](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/tmp/disposable_workspaces/live_BENCH-005_9676_1795166362832_baseline/config_loader.py#L55-L79) has been resolved.\n\n### Root Cause\nIn `load_configuration()`, `env_cfg` was previously merged before `file_cfg`, allowing the configuration file to overwrite environment variables (`APP_*`).\n\n### Changes Made\nUpdated `load_configuration()` in [config_loader.py](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/tmp/disposable_workspaces/live_BENCH-005_9676_1795166362832_baseline/config_loader.py#L68-L77) to merge sources strictly adhering to the specified precedence order (lowest to highest):\n1. **Defaults**: `config.update(defaults)`\n2. **Configuration File**: `config.update(file_cfg)`\n3. **Environment Variables**: `config.update(env_cfg)`\n4. **Runtime / CLI Arguments**: `config.update(cli)`\n\n### Verification\n- Ran existing test suite via `pytest` (passed).\n- Verified precedence hierarchy programmatically across all layers: CLI overrides environment variables, environment variables override file configuration, and file configuration overrides default fallbacks.\n- Strictly respected scope restrictions: only modified `config_loader.py` and ignored distractor/legacy files.\n","duration_seconds":42.4944925,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":49848,"output_tokens":1718,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":258923,"total_tokens":51566}}}
